All 15 tests pass. Here's a summary of the 10 bugs fixed across 3 files:

**`src/auth.py` (2 bugs)**
- `has_permission`: case-sensitive comparison → added `.lower()` on both sides
- `is_admin_or_owner`: used `and` instead of `or` → changed to `or`

**`src/inventory.py` (4 bugs)**
- `__init__`: mutable default `= {}` shared state across instances → `None` default with `dict(initial)` copy
- `add`: `self._stock[sku] = qty` overwrote instead of accumulating → `self._stock.get(sku, 0) + qty`
- `reserve`: `>=` rejected reserving exactly the available amount → changed to `>`
- `release`: allowed reserved count to go negative → added guard that raises `ValueError` if `qty > current`

**`src/text_utils.py` (3 bugs)**
- `slugify`: didn't lowercase characters → `char.lower()` when appending
- `slugify`: `replace("--", "-")` only collapses one pair, leaving `"---"` → `re.sub(r"-+", "-", ...)`
- `truncate`: `text[:max_len] + suffix` exceeded `max_len` → `text[:max_len - len(suffix)] + suffix`
